 due course at a time that is in the public interest. As it will be released soon, the Greens will not be supporting this motion today, in order to allow the government to undertake the necessary processes to ensure this report is released at an appropriate time. We encourage the government to continue communicating openly about the progress of this report and its release date. Katy Gallagher I seek leave to make a short statement. Sue Lines Leave is granted for one minute. Katy Gallagher The government will be opposing this motion. We are working in close consultation with patient, consumer and industry representatives regarding the Health Technology Assessment Review and have commenced negotiations on the strategic agreement. We are progressing the release of the HTA review and continuing to engage with consumers on these reforms, and it's important that these processes be allowed to play out. We'll have more to say on these matters as the process progresses. Sue Lines The question is that general business notic","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10664","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-08-13/5"}
